# tools/purpose-apps/imagenology.apps — what the Medical Imaging purpose is
# supposed to contain, stated once, at the level where drift is a real bug.
#
# The two projects deliver the same purpose by different means and that is
# CORRECT: Carino Setup targets ~40 mutable distros plus Windows and macOS, so
# it reaches for Flatpak wherever a name is not portable; Custom Images builds
# one immutable Fedora, where things belong in /usr as RPMs. Comparing package
# names would therefore flag good decisions as errors. Comparing *applications*
# does not — "Medical Imaging includes a DICOM viewer" is a fact about the
# purpose, while "it arrives as io.github.nroduit.Weasis" is a fact about the
# delivery target.
#
# Format, pipe separated:
#
#   app | setup tokens | image tokens | policy | why
#
#   app     short identity, unique in this file
#   tokens  the names that side WOULD use, space separated alternatives —
#           filled in whether or not that side ships the app today, because an
#           empty column can never notice the gap being closed. The app counts
#           as present on a side if ANY of that side's tokens appears there.
#   policy  both        must be present on both sides    (asymmetry = drift)
#           setup-only  deliberately absent from the image
#           image-only  deliberately absent from Setup
#   why     required for setup-only / image-only; empty for both
#
# Every token either project actually ships must appear somewhere in this file.
# A token claimed by no row is reported as UNMAPPED and fails --strict, so this
# manifest cannot silently go stale the moment either side gains a package.

# --- DICOM toolchain: the shared core, present on both sides today -----------
dcmtk        | dcmtk                | dcmtk                        | both |
gdcm         | python3-gdcm gdcm libgdcm-tools | gdcm gdcm-applications | both |
pydicom      | python3-pydicom      | python3-pydicom              | both |
pynetdicom   | python3-pynetdicom   | python3-pynetdicom           | both |
dcm2niix     | dcm2niix             | dcm2niix                     | both |
nibabel      | python3-nibabel      | python3-nibabel              | both |

# --- Viewers: the purpose is not usable without one --------------------------
# A study can be parsed with the toolchain above but not looked at. Setup
# installs three viewers and xmedcon; the image ships Weasis as a first-boot
# flatpak (its row is clean). The remaining rows are deliberately left as
# violations rather than exempted — the image column carries the name the
# image would use, so each flips to clean the moment the package phase adds it.
weasis       | io.github.nroduit.Weasis | io.github.nroduit.Weasis | both |
aliza        | com.github.AlizaMedicalImaging.AlizaMS | com.github.AlizaMedicalImaging.AlizaMS | both |
invesalius   | br.gov.cti.invesalius | br.gov.cti.invesalius       | both |
xmedcon      | xmedcon              | xmedcon                      | both |

# --- Scientific Python: image-only, and correctly so -------------------------
# The image pins one Fedora release, so numpy/scipy/matplotlib resolve to a
# known-good set at build time. Setup would have to carry per-family names
# across ~40 distros for a stack most of its profiles do not need, and pip or a
# venv is the better answer on a mutable system. The Setup column is still
# filled so the check fires if that decision is ever quietly reversed.
numpy        | python3-numpy        | python3-numpy                | image-only | per-distro naming across the Setup matrix; venv/pip is the better fit on a mutable system
scipy        | python3-scipy        | python3-scipy                | image-only | as numpy
matplotlib   | python3-matplotlib   | python3-matplotlib           | image-only | as numpy

# --- Display calibration: image-only, and load-bearing -----------------------
# Calibration is a property of a fixed, known display attached to a known OS
# image. Setup cannot assume either, so shipping the tooling there would imply
# a guarantee it has no way to keep.
argyllcms    | argyllcms argyll     | argyllcms                    | image-only | calibration presumes a fixed display and a reproducible OS image; Setup can assume neither
colord-icc   | colord-extra-profiles | colord-extra-profiles       | image-only | ships alongside argyllcms
